## Row

::: {.card .decision-card}
## Executive conclusion

<div class="decision-note">{{ thesis }}</div>

{{ h2_statement }}

The queue is a structured review aid—not an automatic replacement approval. It combines
lifecycle timing, absolute availability, peer-relative availability, data confidence,
transparent tiers and threshold sensitivity. It uses neither a composite score nor a
replacement classifier.

<button class="download-report" id="download-standalone-report" type="button">Download offline report</button>
<span class="download-status" id="report-download-status" aria-live="polite"></span>
<script>
(() => {
  const button = document.getElementById("download-standalone-report");
  const status = document.getElementById("report-download-status");
  if (!button) return;
  button.addEventListener("click", () => {
    button.disabled = true;
    if (status) status.textContent = "Preparing download…";
    window.setTimeout(() => {
      const clone = document.documentElement.cloneNode(true);
      const clonedExplorer = clone.querySelector(".explorer-shell");
      if (clonedExplorer) {
        const mount = document.createElement("div");
        mount.id = "fleet-explorer-offline";
        clonedExplorer.replaceWith(mount);
      }
      clone.querySelectorAll("bslib-tooltip, .tooltip, .popover").forEach(node => node.remove());
      clone.querySelectorAll("[aria-describedby]").forEach(node => node.removeAttribute("aria-describedby"));
      const clonedStatus = clone.querySelector("#report-download-status");
      if (clonedStatus) clonedStatus.textContent = "";
      const markup = "<!DOCTYPE html>\n" + clone.outerHTML;
      const url = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([markup], {type: "text/html;charset=utf-8"}));
      const anchor = document.createElement("a");
      anchor.href = url;
      anchor.download = "fleet_replacement_report.html";
      anchor.hidden = true;
      document.body.append(anchor);
      anchor.click();
      anchor.remove();
      window.setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(url), 1000);
      button.disabled = false;
      if (status) status.textContent = "Report downloaded.";
    }, 0);
  });
})();
</script>
:::

::: {.card .recommendation-card}
## Management recommendation

1. Retain the current program if its lifecycle alignment remains operationally valid.
2. Run a quarterly exception review beginning with urgent and high-tier candidates.
3. Route younger poor performers to reliability investigation, not capital replacement.
4. Keep overdue reliable vehicles in lifecycle planning.
5. Repair source-field alignment and define usage measures before right-sizing.
:::

