## Decision framework

Replacement-condition admission requires: operational and outside the program; valid
lifecycle and high-confidence availability; at/beyond expected life or due within two
years; availability below 80%; and bottom-20% peer availability.

Peers use unit type plus expected life at n≥30, fall back to unit type at n≥30, and
otherwise receive no percentile. High priority only escalates a tier. Pareto fronts
order candidates across lifecycle consumption, absolute availability and peer percentile.
:::

::: {.card}
## Data-confidence controls

All source columns are ingested as text with hashes and row lineage. Typed fields never
overwrite raw values. Exact duplicates are collapsed analytically; conflicting duplicate
IDs are quarantined. Suspected displacement is never repaired speculatively.

Availability is explicitly a **proxy**. Usage, expected usage and VEU do not affect actions.

### Availability-confidence robustness

The expanded definition recalculates peers after adding Medium-confidence availability.
It is a robustness comparison only and does not change the primary High-confidence queue.

